# Release configuration for deploy/release.sh.
#
# Copy this file to .config/remo/deploy.env, keep it private (chmod 600), and replace
# the values. The script reads it as data — plain KEY=VALUE lines, no shell — and
# refuses a file it does not own, a file others can read, or a symlink.
REMO_DEPLOY_HOST=deploy@your-host
REMO_APP_ORIGIN=https://boards.example.com
REMO_DOCS_ORIGIN=https://docs.example.com
# A second installation on one machine also sets its own root, compose project and edge
# alias (ADR-261). Leave them out for the default /srv/remo, project `remo`, alias
# `remo-web`.
# REMO_DEPLOY_ROOT=/srv/stage-ru
# REMO_COMPOSE_PROJECT=stage-ru
# REMO_WEB_ALIAS=stage-ru-web
# The release script's public checks on a host behind basic auth (a test stand). The
# value is `user:password`, handed to curl as an argument and never put in a URL.
# REMO_DEPLOY_HTTP_AUTH=tester1:stand-password
